Quasi-separated morphisms are decent, see Decent Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03M5" data-tag="03M5">68.17.2</a>. For any morphism $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k) \to Y$ where $k$ is a field, the algebraic space $X_ k$ is of finite presentation over $k$ because it is of finite type over $k$ and quasi-separated by Decent Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BB6" data-tag="0BB6">68.14.1</a>.